fix(pip): Read the optic imaging type from the pack's own s3ds_image_type key

The thermal fact for the optice the player actually uses had no engine reachable source: the
PiP module marks only the gauss family with scope_lense_thermal, and the SIG Sauer Echo1 has no
thermal key at all. It is not missing though - the 3DSS module declares the imaging type of
every optic with s3ds_image_type on the optic's own section, using the same enumeration the lens
shaders use (0 none, 1 night vision, 2 thermal, 3 thermal colour). [echo1] carries 3, and
[t12] carries 3, while a plain sight like [tac30] has no such key.

The weapon now reads it from the weapon's own child section, from the mounted scope section when
there is one, and - because a variant weapon's section is wpn_<weapon>_<token> while the optic's
keys stay on the <token> section - by walking the suffixes after each underscore and taking any
that names a real section. That last step is what reaches [echo1] from wpn_rsass_echo1, whose
scope slot is empty because this pack mounts optics as addons rather than through m_scopes.

A suffix can land on a section that is another weapon (wpn_a545_gauss also has a545_gauss), so
the suffix walk reads only the optic identity keys and never the optics geometry: lens FOV and
the dynamic zoom flag keep coming from the weapon's child section or the mounted scope.

imageType >= 2 drives ps_r2_heatvision for the lens frames, imageType == 1 drives
ps_r2_nightvision, and both are logged (img= in the per optic line) so the mapping can be
checked from a log rather than by eye.